 Rupak De, Senior Technical Analyst at LKP Securities 
PNB Housing Finance has given a breakout from a falling wedge pattern on the daily chart, suggesting a strong rise in optimism around the stock. The 20-EMA and 50-EMA are in a bullish crossover, indicating a positive setup.
Besides, the RSI on the daily chart has given a breakout from a falling channel, further supporting the positive outlook. The short-term outlook appears positive, with the stock potentially reaching Rs 1,200. On the lower end, support is placed at Rs 1,100.
Adani Green Energy has given a breakout from a downward consolidation pattern on the daily chart, suggesting a strong rise in optimism around the stock. Additionally, it has reclaimed the 50-EMA on the daily timeframe, confirming an improvement in sentiment. Trading volumes have remained high lately, indicating strong participation.
Besides, the RSI on the daily chart has given a breakout from a falling channel, further supporting the positive outlook. The short-term outlook appears positive, with the stock potentially reaching Rs 1,410. On the lower end, support is placed at Rs 1,300.
Laurus Labs is in a cyclical uptrend, forming higher tops and higher bottoms since April. Dips have been well bought into, keeping the uptrend intact. In its latest move, the stock moved higher after finding support at the 20-EMA. The 20-EMA and 50-EMA are in a bullish crossover, further confirming the positive trend.
The trend continues to remain strong and may extend further. On the higher end, the stock could move towards Rs 2,200, while support is placed at Rs 1,954.
 Sudeep Shah, Head of Technical and Derivatives Research at SBI Securities 
 Leela Palaces Hotels & Resorts | CMP: Rs 602.45 
Leela Palaces Hotels has given a breakout from a horizontal trendline resistance on the daily chart, signalling a potential resumption of the uptrend. The RSI is rising, indicating strengthening bullish momentum, while the MACD line has crossed above the signal line and continues to move higher, supported by expanding green histogram bars. This combination of price action and momentum indicators strengthens the positive outlook.
Further supporting the bullish setup, the ratio line in the Leela Palaces/Nifty Tourism Index ratio chart has also given a fresh breakout, highlighting strong relative outperformance within its index. Sustained trading above the breakout zone could keep the bullish bias intact and support further upside in the near term.
Hence, accumulation is recommended in the Rs 595–605 zone, with a stop-loss at Rs 580. On the upside, the stock is likely to test Rs 650 in the short term.
 Multi Commodity Exchange of India | CMP: Rs 3,362.6 
